>>
Rule 1 (input and other tensors must have compatible dtypes for multiplication)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) = dtype_(v_2)
>>
Rule 2 (input and other tensors should have compatible shapes for broadcasting)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 0 ∧ ndim(v_2) ≥ 0 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, if ndim(v_1) ≥ ndim(v_2) then ndim(v_1) - 1 else ndim(v_2) - 1] : if ndim(v_1) - i - 1 ≥ 0 ∧ ndim(v_2) - i - 1 ≥ 0 then (shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - i - 1) = shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) - i - 1) ∨ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - i - 1) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) - i - 1) = 1)
>>
Rule 3 (input and other tensors must have a number of dimensions less than or equal to a limit)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≤ 8 ∧ ndim(v_2) ≤ 8
>>
Rule 4 (if input is complex, other must also be complex)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 10 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 11 then dtype_(v_2) = 10 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 11
>>
Rule 5 (input and other tensors must have at least one dimension)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 1 ∧ ndim(v_2) ≥ 1
>>
Rule 6 (If one tensor is boolean, the other must also be boolean.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 0 then dtype_(v_2) = 0 else if dtype_(v_2) = 0 then dtype_(v_1) = 0
>>
Rule 7 (The number of elements in at least one dimension must be positive)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= (ndim(v_1) = 0) ∨ (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0) ∧ (ndim(v_2) = 0) ∨ (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : shape(v_2, i) > 0)
>>
Rule 8 (If the first tensor is a scalar, the second one must not be a boolean)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 0 then dtype_(v_2) ≠ 0
>>
Rule 9 (If the first tensor is complex, the second one must be a number.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 10 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 11 then (dtype_(v_2) = 1 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 2 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 3 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 4 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 5 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 8 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 9 ∨ ndim(v_2) = 0)
>>
Rule 10 (If one tensor is a scalar and the other is not, the scalar tensor must have a compatible type)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if (ndim(v_1) = 0 ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0) then (dtype_(v_1) = 1 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 2 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 3 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 4 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 5 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 8 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 9 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 0) else if (ndim(v_2) = 0 ∧ ndim(v_1) > 0) then (dtype_(v_2) = 1 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 2 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 3 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 4 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 5 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 8 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 9 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 0)
>>
Rule 11 (If one of the tensors is of integer type, the other should not be a complex type)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if (dtype_(v_1) = 1 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 2 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 3 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 4 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 5) then (dtype_(v_2) ≠ 10 ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≠ 11) else if (dtype_(v_2) = 1 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 2 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 3 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 4 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 5) then (dtype_(v_1) ≠ 10 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≠ 11)
>>
Rule 12 (If the first tensor is a float, the second must not be bool)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if (dtype_(v_1) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 8 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 9) then dtype_(v_2) ≠ 0
>>
Rule 13 (If the first tensor is bool, the second tensor should have a single element.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 0 then (ndim(v_2) = 0 ∨ (ndim(v_2) = 1 ∧ shape(v_2, 0) = 1) ∨ (ndim(v_2) = 2 ∧ shape(v_2, 0) = 1 ∧ shape(v_2, 1) = 1))
>>
Rule 14 (If one of the tensors is complex, then both must be complex, float, or integer tensors)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if (dtype_(v_1) = 10 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 11) then (dtype_(v_2) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 8 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 9 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 1 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 2 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 3 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 4 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 5 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 10 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 11) else if (dtype_(v_2) = 10 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 11) then (dtype_(v_1) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 8 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 9 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 1 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 2 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 3 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 4 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 5 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 10 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 11)
>>
Rule 15 (If v_1 is float16/float32/float64/complex64/complex128, then v_2 must be a number or the same type as v_1)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 8 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 9 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 10 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 11 then dtype_(v_2) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 8 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 9 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 10 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 11 ∨ ndim(v_2) = 0
>>
Rule 16 (If one of the tensors has a size of zero on at least one dimension, the result of the multiplication is likely to be a tensor with at least one dimension with zero size.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = 0) ∨ (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : shape(v_2, i) = 0) then true
>>
Rule 17 (if one tensor is complex, the other tensor must have matching complex type or be a float/int.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 10 then (dtype_(v_2) = 10 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 1 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 2 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 3 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 4 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 5 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 8 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 9) else if dtype_(v_1) = 11 then (dtype_(v_2) = 11 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 1 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 2 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 3 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 4 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 5 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 8 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 9) else if dtype_(v_2) = 10 then (dtype_(v_1) = 10 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 1 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 2 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 3 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 4 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 5 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 8 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 9) else if dtype_(v_2) = 11 then (dtype_(v_1) = 11 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 1 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 2 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 3 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 4 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 5 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 8 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 9)
>>
Rule 18 (If any dimension in either of the tensor is very large, the result might overflow)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= (∃i ∈ [0, if ndim(v_1) > 0 then ndim(v_1) -1 else 0] : shape(v_1, i) > 1000000) ∨ (∃i ∈ [0, if ndim(v_2) > 0 then ndim(v_2) - 1 else 0] : shape(v_2, i) > 1000000)
>>
Rule 19 (If one of the tensor is of bool dtype, then the other tensor must be scalar of int/float/bool, or be a tensor of bool)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 0 then ((ndim(v_2) = 0) ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 0 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 1 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 2 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 3 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 4 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 5 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 8 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 9) else if dtype_(v_2) = 0 then ((ndim(v_1) = 0) ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 0 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 1 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 2 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 3 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 4 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 5 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 8 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 9)
>>
Rule 20 (For high precision, if one of tensors if float64/complex128 the other must have at least float32/complex64 )
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 9 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 11 then (dtype_(v_2) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 8 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 9 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 10 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 11) else if dtype_(v_2) = 9 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 11 then (dtype_(v_1) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 8 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 9 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 10 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 11)
>>
Rule 21 (If the tensors are not scalar, then their number of elements must be greater than 0.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= (ndim(v_1) = 0 ∨ ∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0) ∧ (ndim(v_2) = 0 ∨ ∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : shape(v_2, i) > 0)
